From: Thomas Steiner <tomac@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:04:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] [iOS] Continue Gemma answers that the background
 interrupts

iOS stops GPU work in the background, so a GPU turn stops when the
browser goes there. A turn whose answer had partly reached the page
failed so far. It now goes on in the foreground where it stopped, and
the page gets one answer.

LiteRT-LM conversations only take whole turns. The continuation renders
the conversation in Gemma's prompt format with the model's turn left
open after the partial answer, and decodes from there in a session that
applies no template. That session comes from LiteRT-LM's C API, through
an accessor for the native engine that fetch.py adds to Engine.swift.
Conversations with images or audio, and turns with a response schema,
keep the old behavior. On an iPhone 11 Pro Max, an answer interrupted
mid-sentence continued with the next word.
